<%= render 'controls' %>
<section class="card">
  <h2>Eleven filters, exact shared presets</h2>
  <p>Matching and Non-matching columns evaluate immutable reference contexts. Current follows this browser’s controls.
    All columns use the published SDK against the currently loaded definitions.</p>
  <% matching = flags_for(RequestContext.build(RequestContext::PRESETS.fetch('matching'))) %>
  <% other = flags_for(RequestContext.build(RequestContext::PRESETS.fetch('non-matching'))) %>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <caption>Native outcomes; package limitations remain visible</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Filter</th>
          <th>Matching</th>
          <th>Non-matching</th>
          <th>Current</th>
          <th>What to expect</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% Catalog::FILTERS.each do |suffix, name, note| %>
          <% key = "filter-#{suffix}" %>
          <tr data-filter="<%= key %>">
            <td><strong><%= name %></strong><br><code><%= key %></code></td>
            <td><%= state_badge(matching.fetch(key)) %></td>
            <td><%= state_badge(other.fetch(key)) %></td>
            <td><%= state_badge(feature_enabled?(key)) %></td>
            <td><%= note %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Reference native results with the shared fixture: Targeting is ON/ON; Macintosh DeviceType is OFF/OFF.
    The rules remain unchanged. Percentage may be the same for both identities. No extra denial rule or replacement parser is introduced.</p>
</section>
